// @test: a `lit(...)` as the FIRST component of a multi-value return serializes raw (#427 defect 8)
// @description: the mirror image of test_lit_component_multivalue_return.vyb --
//   `main()<Int, String> -> { return lit(1), "x" }` asserted in
//   `CreateSExtOrTrunc: Can only sign extend/truncate integers!` (exit 134), because the declared
//   element type for slot 0 is Int while the value reaching the serializer is lit()'s raw
//   serialized i8*. Both directions are now the same fix: a bare-pointer component is emitted
//   verbatim. The ordinary component ("x") still goes through JSON escaping, so the array reads
//   `[1, "x"]` -- raw for the literal, quoted for the value.
// @category: serialization
// @expect-return: [1, "x"]

main()<Int, String> -> {
    return lit(1), "x"
}
